  "evidence": [
    "Pinned audio lifecycle bodies inline base constructor/destructor stages: Sound4C6080, Wave4C66E0/4C67C0, Midi4C75B0/4C7670, Ambience4C8460. Existing real class hierarchy supplies the correct owners; lack of TU visibility prevents those stages in the current build.",
    "Read-only native compiler controls on df3f94c33: header-only inlining loses standalone symbol emission. Co-located definitions with explicit inline Sound destructor retain standalone lifetimes and emit the pinned base-to-derived table sequence, with no manual table writes. pragma function(memset) restores original calls and measured root4C8410 exactness; existing frame profile preserves Sound deleting destructor4C92D0. Complete shared unwind spans still refuse rather than pass.",
    "Authorize complete mapping/history/body moves into existing Sound owner, preserving bug-for-bug body statements, hierarchy, objects, original identities and claims. Keep global storage and startup ownership unchanged. Region-limit memset policy and measure the whole family. Adopt only demonstrated per-TU inlining/frame recipe and aligned application setting if needed; no whole-project flag changes.",
    "Coordinator permits scoped temporary matching regressions for this evidence-backed lifetime-visibility migration; preserve historical obligations and explicitly enumerate any regression. Require fresh full build/link, mapping/claim/reference checks, physical lifecycle references and relevant behavior/conservation tests before manual integration. No full-game or automatic acceptance claim. Tests may migrate source-host expectations but must preserve behavior and historical conservation checks."
  ],
  "intent": "Recover shared audio lifecycle visibility through genuine co-located class definitions while preserving all original mappings and standalone lifetime emission.",
